<title>UK: Ceval Alimentos plans $100 mln Eurobond - dealers.</title>
<headline>Ceval Alimentos plans $100 mln Eurobond - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian food processing company Ceval Alimentos plans to issue a $100 million Eurobond next week, syndicate managers said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The deal will have an eight-year maturity with puts and calls after five years. Spread talk was around 425 basis points over the put. Chase was tipped as lead manager.</p>
<p>Ceval Alimentos last tapped the Eurobond market in September when it issued a $100 million eight-year bond with puts and calls after three years.</p>
<p>That deal was launched via Citibank.</p>
<p>-- Aline van Duyn, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
